@{
ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="privacy-page">

<div class="privacy-header">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Attendance Management System</p>
</div>

<div class="privacy-card">

    <h2>About Your Data</h2>

    <p>
        The Attendance Management System (AMS) is designed to help manage
        student information, modules and attendance records.
    </p>

    <p>
        The system may store information such as student names, student
        numbers, email addresses, courses, year of study and attendance
        records.
    </p>

    <h2>How Your Information Is Used</h2>

    <p>
        Information stored within the system is used for educational and
        administrative purposes, including managing student enrolment,
        recording attendance and producing attendance reports.
    </p>

    <h2>Who Can Access Your Information?</h2>

    <p>
        Access to information is restricted according to the user's role.
        Module Leaders may access information required to manage their
        modules and student attendance. Students should only be able to
        access information relating to themselves.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping Your Information Secure</h2>

    <p>
        The system uses user authentication and role-based access controls
        to help prevent unauthorised access to student information.
    </p>

    <p>
        Users should keep their login credentials private and should log
        out of the system when they have finished using it.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
        Student and attendance information should only be retained for as
        long as it is required for legitimate educational or administrative
        purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
        If you have questions about how your information is stored or used,
        please contact the appropriate member of staff or system
        administrator.
    </p>

</div>

</div>
